Package: libva-v4l2-stateful
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: VA-API driver for V4L2 stateful video decoders (Diting iris)
 VA-API backend on top of V4L2 stateful (memory-to-memory) decoders,
 patched for the Qualcomm iris decoder of the Xiaomi 12T Pro (diting):
 H.264, HEVC and VP9 hardware decoding for VA-API applications.
 .
 Also installed as msm_drv_video.so, the name libva derives from the msm
 DRM driver, so applications use it without LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME.
 .
 Firefox works directly. Snap Chromium cannot read host libraries: a
 systemd user service copies the driver into ~/snap/chromium/common/dri
 at login (see diting-chromium-vaapi).
